	abstract = {The proceedings contain 13 papers. The topics discussed include: reciprocal collision avoidance for quadrotor helicopters using LQR-obstacles; towards optimization-based multi-agent collision-avoidance under continuous stochastic dynamics; learning conflicts from experience; towards using discrete multiagent pathfinding to address continuous problems; positioning to win: a dynamic role assignment and formation positioning system; non-optimal multi-agent pathfinding is solved (since 1984); conflict-based search for optimal multi-agent path finding; reciprocal collision avoidance and multi-agent navigation for video games; independence detection for multi-agent pathflnding problems; and time optimal multi-agent path planning on graphs.},
