	abstract = {The proceedings contain 12 papers. The topics discussed include: a multi-path compilation approach to contingent planning; making reasonable assumptions to plan with incomplete information: abridged report; learning interactions among objects through spatio-temporal reasoning; a planning-based approach for generating planning problems; using classical planners for plan verification and counterexample generation; planning with global constraints for computing infrastructure reconfiguration; using planning for a personalized security agent; composition of flow-based applications with HTN planning; using classical planners to solve conformant probabilistic planning problems; solving goal hybrid Markov decision processes using numeric classical planners; and planning the transformation of network topologies.},
